  <CATEGORY Name="Ending">
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_0">!!! VERY IMPORTANT PLEASE READ !!![br][br]These should be placed around parkour_level.hpm as collectables so there's a bit of buildup for the epilogue. Ideally we get Ramen to voice these and auto-play them on pickup so that they don't mess with the pacing.[br][br]NOTE FOR DEVS: We don't have time to port over all the fancy ImGui stuff from SOMA, so just use Debug Action #3 to cycle between notes. Couldn't get the DW tablets working so this is what we're doing.</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_1">COLLECTABLE NOTE #1:[br][br]What is reality? This is a question that I ask myself every day. One minute I am trapped in a bunker with horrors beyond comprehension, and the next I am jumping around like a madman in a city of glass![br][br]I have been to many places, and many times, but this is the most unique. It lies at the outer edge of existence, somewhere between reality and fantasy. Reason and chaos. I hope to one day understand its mysteries.[br][br]-Henri</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_2">COLLECTABLE NOTE #2:[br][br]I have long wondered why this place is called The Hallway of Realities. It is a hallway, no doubt, but it looks like only one reality to me![br][br]Lambert would be laughing at me now. It is a wordplay, a trick. This is the hallway of *realities*: Things that are real. The expression of abstract concepts in literal form. I'm not yet certain what this "debug room" represents, but I am determined to figure it out![br][br]- Henri</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_3">COLLECTABLE NOTE #3:[br][br]The manifestation of the Sitting Room frightens me. Unlike the others, it represents nothing but cold, infinite darkness. It is the world between worlds, the space between spaces. What is not eating away at what is.[br][br]I fear I must brave the Dead Room. My life will be decided by a simple coin toss, it seems. May fate be at my side, and if she falters...[br][br]May my creator welcome me with open arms.[br][br]- Henri</Entry>
	<Entry Name="DebugRoomNote_4">That's it![br][br]We're not going to have much narrative context otherwise, and we really need that in order to hit the theme, so make sure these get added before the deadline!![br][br]-Maurice</Entry>
  </CATEGORY>
</LANGUAGE>
